  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The sharing of 100 million doses of the Covid-19 vaccines with countries in need</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">At the G7 Summit on 11 June 2021 the Prime Minister announced the United Kingdom (UK) will donate 100 million surplus Covid-19 vaccines to the world within a year; 80 million will go through COVAX and 20 million will be donated bilaterally. 5 million of these will be donated by the end of September 2021 and 30 million by the end of 2021.</narrative>
  </description>
